RedoSan Authenticity is a dual-use security research toolkit.

It contains software that can be used for both defensive and offensive
purposes, including watermarking, fingerprinting, forensic analysis and
digital-identity tooling. It is published in accordance with npm's
Dual-Use Content Policy.

Intended uses include: media authenticity verification, provenance
research, digital forensics education, and security testing of content
you own or are authorised to test.

RedoSan Authenticity must not be used to produce forgeries, to impersonate
others, or to violate any applicable law. Users are solely responsible
for how they use this software.

